Z||000000||Alex4mula||05-10-2001||08:35 AM||||Holley manufactures two fuel injection Commander 950 units for SBC V8. One is a MPFI for around $2500 and the other is a TBI for around $1300. Both come with injectors (8 on MPFI & 4 on TBI), computers, sensors and all wires needed. Both handle easily 250Hp to 350HP as minimum in basic model. I know the benefits of MPFI but, for $1200 less the TBI is very attractive. I'm looking for feedback in MPFI vs TBI for this type of application. Not interested if a TPI or other setup is cheaper etc. I know that. Should I see a big difference in throttle response from one to another? This will be for a street engine in the 275 to 330 HP range like a ZZ4 or similar. Thanks.||||reg||1
